      {
        "id": 228877,
        "name": "morph147",
        "username": "morph147",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/m/839c29/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2020-05-17T23:49:09.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"fenianb\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/f/b38774/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> fenianb:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I’m tempted to start a This Day In Prime War History thread. One year ago today Paul Bender said “Lore Forge was in town this week and we made a ton of progress on the rules and playtesting! At this point, you’ll see a very close to final version of the Prime War rules at Gen Con with very preliminary art and graphic design. We are currently planning on having the game ready to send to the printer in Q1 2020.” <a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/comment/201987#comment-201987\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">https://greaterthangames.com/comment/201987#comment-201987</a> So maybe the coming announcement will thrill us all. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p>If you start a This day in prime war history thread it would be filled with a lot of empty void.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Rereading Pauls post reminded me we are in a pandemic and George R.R. Martin better have nothing else to do except write winds of winter. He probably isnt though.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>",
