      {
        "id": 228878,
        "name": "fenianb",
        "username": "fenianb",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/f/b38774/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2020-05-18T13:28:20.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"morph147\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/m/839c29/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> morph147:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p>If you start a This day in prime war history thread it would be filled with a lot of empty void.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Rereading Pauls post reminded me we are in a pandemic and George R.R. Martin better have nothing else to do except write winds of winter. He probably isnt though.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p>We could include the dates for KS launches and shipments for stuff announced after Broken City/For Profit and completed since. Y’know, for perspective. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/wink.png?v=12\" title=\":wink:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":wink:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>As of March 18 Martin says he’s feeling fine, staying safe, and writing in Westeros every day. So there’s hope for ASOIAF fans yet.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>",
